at is the true reason: one task per carrier, scheduler state, a pending wake?) and anything else that is genuinely about the OUTSIDE world (op-ids, custody) at a non-parked pc. (C) What must change: the validator rules (window membership at an arbitrary pc), `lift-state`/`lower-state` refusals, the rows (does an `:act` row carry a pc already; is there a new row kind), the tail-completion seam, the harness laws (what is the matrix at every pc; sampling strategy: every pc of the corpus is how many cases), and the numbering/carrier (does anything depend on parking). (D) Value and cost: what any-pc snapshots buy (time travel, debugging, replay speed, checkpoint at fuel exhaustion, preemption, migration of a running task) versus replay from the last safe point plus a step count (\"derive, don't persist\"); an honest estimate of the slice in opus days plus review rounds (we average 2-4 codex rounds per slice), the order relative to phase 7 and phase 8 (should it come before the cutover so the old engines can serve as cross-check, or after, with the semantic-register kernel alone), and the risks. (E) A recommendation: do it, defer it, or never; if do it, the slice plan (files, acceptance tests named, hosts) in the same shape as the phase 7 plan. Also flag any wording in the owner's argument you disagree with, and give the exact amendment text for the design if you recommend adopting the generalization. Foreground only. Report starts with a 15-line plain summary for the owner and ends with READY or NOT READY (with blocking questions).\n","numLines":7,"startLine":1,"totalLines":7}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CDDqpMS75P6JnG9jpHAhET","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
