fied.** 4b stage 2 is not landed: rows 3-4, 7-12, 17, 24 are\n1636\t  written against the evaluator design's §1.4-1.6 shapes and the stage-1\n1637\t  branch and must be re-read when stage 2 lands. The seam of §4.3 is a\n1638\t  specification of a change to `stack.cljc`, not a reading of code that\n1639\t  exists. **Amended after 6b (2026-10-13):** 4b stage 2 landed before\n1640\t  6b, and rows 3-4, 7-12, 17 and 24 now run on the reference lane (89\n1641\t  labelled row × segment executions, 85 distinct builder/wrapper setups\n1642\t  since rows 3 and 24 share one builder by design); rows 10-11 were\n1643\t  re-read and corrected (§5.2, B1). The 6b harness ran on the JVM only;\n1644\t  Node and Dart execution of `rows.cljc`'s transport and the new harness\n1645\t  file remain the three-host gate of §8.2 item 9, not established by the\n1646\t  reviews.\n1647\t\n1648\t---\n1649\t\n1650\t## 10. Findings and proposed amendments\n1651\t\n1652\tReviewer rulings (codex gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-10-10): F1, F4, U2, U4, U5,\n1653\tR1, R2, R7, C1 **ACCEPT**; F2, F3, U1, U3, U6, R3, R4, R5, R6, R8, R9\n1654\t**ACCEPT WITH CHANGES**, applied below; dropping `:yin.k/engine`\n1655\t**ACCEPTED**; the merged-`E` free environment **REJECTED**, replaced by\n1656\t§4.4/§6.3.\n1657\t\n1658\t### 10.1 To the frozen design (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`)\n1659\t\n1660\t**F1 — §4.2 row names (ACCEPT).** Replace \"`:regs` becomes `[segment-A\n1661\tpc env-cref window-cref k-cref deliver-D]` for an `act` and a sibling\n1662\t`:tail-state [segment-A site k-cref deliver-D]` is added\" with: \"the\n1663\tframe rows are `:act [segment-A pc env-cref window-cref k-cref rd]` and\n1664\t`:tail [segment-A site k-cref]`, the kind being the delivery\n1665\tdiscriminant, so `deliver` is not a slot; `:window` is a keyed row\n1666\t`[r₁ V₁ r₂ V₂ …]` sorted by `r` in which a nil-valued register is a\n1667\tpresent `[:lit nil]`; `:kframe` is `[segment-A pc env-cref window-cref\n1668\trd]`; `:stack` and `stack-base` are removed; the root gains `free-env`,\n1669\tthe task's initial free environment (continuation design §2, §6.3).\"\n1670\t\n1671\t**F2 — §4.2 the validator (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** After \"and pending\n1672\tcompatibility with `reason`\" insert: \"The validator is the pure function\n1673\t`(defect frame code context task)` of `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`\n1674\t§3: `task` is decoded task context (the parked key, the live FFI call\n1675\tids, the free environment), never an engine; its rules are ordered,\n1676\tstructural checks first, current-window rules on `act` only, return\n1677\twindows separately, and every `E` is checked to agree with the task's\n1678\tfree environment off the lexical names; it runs after canonical\n1679\tnumbering, as the carrier orders it.\"\n1680\t\n1681\t**F3 — §4.3 foreign engines (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** After\n1682\t\"`lift(lower(frame)) = frame` holds for admitted canonical frames, as\n1683\ttoday.\" insert: \"The register kernel pairs physical and virtual\n1684\tregisters pc by pc from `v` and `R(v)`, recovers every destination from\n1685\tA's call (its `dest` is physical), and resolves each return frame's\n1686\timage and relative pc independently; the stack kernel corresponds the\n1687\tnon-push instructions of `H(v)` with `v`, slices its operand stack\n1688\t`[previous-base, base_i)` per return frame and `[last-base, count)` for\n1689\tthe current activation, and needs a tail-completion seam to deliver a\n1690\ttail state through `K` (continuation design §4.3, slice 6c-pre); both\n1691\tkernels' positional frames become `E` through the owner chain and\n1692\t`bind-params`, with the task's free environment carried explicitly. The\n1693\tAST walker is not a frame reconstructor.\"\n1694\t\n1695\t**F4 — §10 phase 6 (ACCEPT).** Replace \"the row carrier amended\" with\n1696\t\"the row carrier amended to body version 3 with one profile,\n1697\t`{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`, carrying canonical vectors\n1698\tby A, `:yin.k/trees` and the task's free environment, never a native\n1699\timage (continuation design §2, §6)\"; after \"through their layouts\"\n1700\tinsert \"(the register and stack kernels, the latter with its\n1701\ttail-completion seam; the walker is excluded)\".\n1702\t\n1703\t### 10.2 To UCF (`yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md`)\n1704\t\n1705\t**U1 — §7.3.4 `:505-527` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace `:511`\n1706\t\"`:yin.k/carried` carries vectors, not batches.\" with \"`:yin.k/carried`\n1707\tand the body's code map carry **register-shaped canonical vectors keyed\n1708\tby A**, never batches, never datoms projected from a vector, and never a\n1709\tnative stack or register image: a receiver of either native kernel\n1710\tderives its image from A (derivations design §2-3). `:yin.k/requires\n1711\t:yin.k/trees` maps every address in `:yin.k/segments` to the non-empty\n1712\tset of tree addresses the emitter's `source-index` held for it\n1713\t(derivations design §9.2).\" **Replace `:513-527`** (\"Loading a fetched\n1714\tvector has two paths … nothing may depend on which path a conforming\n1715\tengine takes.\") with: \"Loading a fetched vector has **one path**: the\n1716\tdirect decode of the canonical vector into an image through the one\n1717\tvalidator (`yin.vm.semantic-register.code/well-formed?`). The projection\n1718\tpath (vector → datoms → loader) is retired (owner ruling 2026-09-18;\n1719\t`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §3.4). The conformance obligation is\n1720\tthat the two AST projection lanes and the direct vector load yield one\n1721\timage and address (`load_paths_test.cljc`).\"\n1722\t\n1723\t**U2 — §7.4.1 (ACCEPT).** At its head: \"Superseded for the\n1724\tregister-shaped machine by `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §4.1 (two\n1725\tstate columns, `act` and `tail`, and the `deliver` record); the table\n1726\tbelow describes the stack-shaped machine, which leaves at that design's\n1727\tphase 8.\" Replace the `:yin.k/frame