Window values, environments,\n1755\t`K` and physical layouts are not claimed\"; replace \"physical slot →\n1756\tcanonical slot\" with \"physical location → virtual register\n1757\t(continuation design §4)\".\n1758\t\n1759\t**U4 — §7.4.3 (ACCEPT).** After \"Three rules make these resumable\":\n1760\t\"A pending rides on an `act` state (write-result delivery) or a `tail`\n1761\tstate (through-return delivery); the variants are unchanged, and\n1762\t`:yin.k/registers R` of the version-2 amendment is the `act`/`tail`\n1763\tstate of the frozen design §4.2.\"\n1764\t\n1765\t**U5 — §7.6 (ACCEPT).** In §7.6.1's example add\n1766\t`:yin.k/trees {A #{tree-address …}}  ; §7.6.1a` and a new §7.6.1a with\n1767\tthe phase-5 §9.2 UCF row text verbatim, including its completeness\n1768\tclause (absent or empty is incomplete).\n1769\t\n1770\t**U6 — §7.11 (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** In \"Safepoint conformance\n1771\tharness\" replace \"including `lift ∘ lower = id`, the static\n1772\t`stack-effect`/`lexically-required` checks\" with \"including `lift ∘\n1773\tlower = id` on canonical frames, the static `def`/`use`/`live` and\n1774\t`lexically-required` checks, the frame validator on every frame, and\n1775\t**cross-engine canonical equality**: one program at one safepoint lifts\n1776\tto row sets with equal root ids after the harness's specified\n1777\tre-emission (continuation design §5.5) from the semantic-register kernel\n1778\tand from the stack and register kernels through their layouts, the stack\n1779\tkernel with its tail-completion seam\". In §7.11.1 \"Safepoint\n1780\treconstruction\", replace \"Separately prepare two independently\n1781\timplemented UCF engines\" with \"Separately prepare the three engines\n1782\tintended to reconstruct canonical frames (the semantic-register kernel;\n1783\tthe register kernel; the stack kernel after its tail-completion seam)\"\n1784\tand \"the frame, pending wait, next result, and effect trace must agree\n1785\tin both directions\" with \"the canonical row set after re-emission, the\n1786\tpending wait, next result and effect trace must agree across all three\n1787\tand in every lowering direction\".\n1788\t\n1789\t### 10.3 To the row-carrier draft (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`)\n1790\t\n1791\tThe inventory below is every clause the grep of the draft for\n1792\t\"legacy\", \"version 0/1/2\", \"semantic profile only / semantic-only\",\n1793\t\"does not translate\", \"unchanged / do not move\", \"other profile\",\n1794\t\"registry\" found operative; each is replaced or deleted.\n1795\t\n1796\t**R1 — §2 `:50-81` (ACCEPT).** Replace the section with: \"**Body\n1797\tversion 3, one profile.** The carrier is body version 3 and reads no\n1798\tother version (owner, 2026-10-11: no legacy): a body of version 0, 1 or\n1799\t2 is `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` at the gate and is never normalised or\n1800\tupgraded. The profile map is `{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`;\n1801\tthere is no engine key, because the frame is the canonical\n1802\tregister-shaped machine's and the executing kernel is the receiving\n1803\tcomposition's choice: the stack and register kernels lower the same rows\n1804\tthrough their layouts (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`\n1805\t§2.1, §4). Any other profile map is `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`.\"\n1806\t\n1807\t**R1a — status paragraph `:18-20`.** Replace \"Body versions 0, 1 and 2\n1808\tkeep their grammar, readers and bytes; this document proposes a fourth\n1809\tbody version whose carrier is rows\" with \"This document specifies body\n1810\tversion 3, the one carrier; older bodies are not read.\"\n1811\t\n1812\t**R2 — §5.2 `:298-317` (ACCEPT).** Replace with continuation §2.3's\n1813\ttable and notes.\n1814\t\n1815\t**R3 — §5.1 `:287-296` (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace the `:reified`\n1816\trow with `| :reified | act-cref | a captured continuation: the decoded\n1817\tact state of frozen §4.2, no pending |`; replace \"`{:yin.k/tag\n1818\t:yin.k/frame :yin.k/regis