{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012GxWwnfgD8pYuFceU1RBf3","type":"tool_result","content":"400\t;; Return transitions & restore\n401\t;; =============================================================================\n402\t\n403\t(defn- return-transition\n404\t  \"Unified return transition: restores caller frame from continuation if\n405\t   pending, otherwise halts the VM with `val`. Only pc, frames, registers,\n406\t   and continuation are restored (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, r7): a\n407\t   frame carries no code space, so an image attached while the call was\n408\t   in flight stays attached, and the absolute `:return-pc` still names\n409\t   the caller's instruction in the grown code space.\"\n410\t  [vm val]\n411\t  (let [continuation (:continuation vm)]\n412\t    (if (seq continuation)\n413\t      (let [frame (peek continuation)\n414\t            return-pc (:return-pc frame)\n415\t            body (body-of-pc (:segment vm) return-pc)\n416\t            reg-count (:registers body)\n417\t            dest (:dest frame)\n418\t            restored-regs (reduce (fn [acc [r v]] (assoc acc r v))\n419\t                                  (vec (repeat reg-count nil))\n420\t                                  (:regs frame))\n421\t            final-regs (if (some? dest)\n422\t                         (assoc restored-regs dest val)\n423\t                         restored-regs)]\n424\t        (assoc vm\n425\t               :pc return-pc\n426\t               :frames (:frames frame)\n427\t               :registers final-regs\n428\t               :continuation (pop continuation)\n429\t               :store-of (:store-of frame)\n430\t               :value val\n431\t               :halted? false))\n432\t      (assoc vm :halted? true, :value val, :store-of nil))))\n433\t\n434\t\n435\t(defn- refuse-continuation!\n436\t  [base entry]\n437\t  (throw (ex-info \"Cannot restore a continuation of another model or image\"\n438\t                  {:reason :foreign-format,\n439\t                   :rule :continuation-format,\n440\t                   :format (:format entry),\n441\t                   :hash (:hash entry),\n442\t                   :image (:image entry),\n443\t                   :expected-format format-tag,\n444\t                   :expected-hash (:hash base),\n445\t                   :images (:images base)})))\n446\t\n447\t\n448\t(defn- check-format!\n449\t  \"Refuse `entry` unless it is this model's payload for a row of the offset\n450\t   table (r6).\"\n451\t  [base entry]\n452\t  (when-not (and (= format-tag (:format entry))\n453\t                 (some #(= (:image entry) (nth % 0)) (:images base)))\n454\t    (refuse-continuation! base entry)))\n455\t\n456\t\n457\t(defn- write-back\n458\t  \"Write `entry`'s registers back and deliver `val` via `:write-result` or\n459\t   `:return-result`. Registers only: `:segment` is kernel state.\"\n460\t  [base entry val]\n461\t  (if (= :return-result (:resume-mode entry))\n462\t    (return-transition (assoc base\n463\t                              :pc (:pc entry)\n464\t                              :frames (:frames entry)\n465\t                              :continuation (:continuation entry)\n466\t                              :store-of (:store-of entry)\n467\t                              :halted? false)\n468\t                       val)\n469\t    (let [pc (:pc entry)\n470\t          body (body-of-pc (:segment base) pc)\n471\t          reg-count (:registers body)\n472\t          dest (:dest entry)\n473\t          restored-regs\n474\t          (reduce (fn [acc [r v]] (assoc acc r v))\n475\t                  (vec (repeat reg-count nil))\n476\t                  (:regs entry))\n477\t          final-regs (if (some? dest)\n478\t                       (assoc restored-regs dest val)\n479\t                       restored-regs)]\n480\t      (assoc base\n481\t             :pc pc\n482\t             :frames (:frames entry)\n483\t             :registers final-regs\n484\t             :continuation (:continuation entry)\n485\t             :store-of (:store-of entry)\n486\t             :value val\n487\t             :halted? false))))\n488\t\n489\t\n490\t(defn register-restore\n491\t  \"The register VM's restore function, `base entry val -> state`\n492\t   (design section 5.2.3). Validates format identity and that the entry's\n493\t   `:image` is a row of the offset table (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3,\n494\t   r6; `:hash` is never a restore key, since it changes at every\n495\t   `attach-image`), checks that the payload is defect-free via\n496\t   effects/continuation-defect, checks that `val` is plain data, handles\n497\t   the FFI two-step, and delivers `val` via `:write-result` or\n498\t   `:return-result`. The entry restores registers only and never assigns\n499\t   `:segment`: the code space is kernel state.\"\n500\t  [base entry val]\n501\t  (check-format! base entry)\n502\t  (when-let [defect (effects/continuation-defect entry)]\n503\t    (throw (ex-info \"Corrupt or tampered continuation payload\"\n504\t                    defect)))\n505\t  (when-not (vm/machine-data? val)\n506\t    (throw (ex-info \"Resume value must be plain data\"\n507\t                    {:rule :resume-value, :val val})))\n508\t  (if (:request-sent entry)\n509\t    (-> base\n510\t        (update :wait-set (fnil conj [])\n511\t                (ffi/response-wait-entry entry (:call-id entry)))\n512\t        (assoc :value :yin/blocked\n513\t               :blocked? true\n514\t               :halted? false))\n515\t    (let [call-id (:call-id entry)\n516\t          base (if call-id (update base :parked dissoc call-id) base)\n517\t          val (if call-id (ffi/call-result val call-id) val)]\n518\t      (write-back base entry val))))\n519\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7716a8d-bcb9-4b49-9ad0-ed6a5daed388","uuid":"25e2a48a-c70c-4121-b46c-12339b8067be","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:48:01.458Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc","content":";; Return transitions & restore\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- return-transition\n  \"Unified return transition: restores caller frame from continuation if\n   pending, otherwise halts the VM with `val`. Only pc, frames, registers,\n   and continuation are restored (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, r7): a\n   frame carries no code space, so an image attached while the call was\n   in flight stays attached, and the absolute `:return-pc` still names\n   the caller's instruction in the grown code space.\"\n  [vm val]\n  (let [continuation (:continuation vm)]\n    (if (seq continuation)\n      (let [frame (peek continuation)\n            return-pc (:return-pc frame)\n            body (body-of-pc (:segment vm) return-pc)\n            reg-count (:registers body)\n            dest (:dest frame)\n            restored-regs (reduce (fn [acc [r v]] (assoc acc r v))\n                                  (vec (repeat reg-count nil))\n                                  (:regs frame))\n            final-regs (if (some? dest)\n                         (assoc restored-regs dest val)\n                         restored-regs)]\n        (assoc vm\n               :pc return-pc\n               :frames (:frames frame)\n               :registers final-regs\n               :continuation (pop continuation)\n               :store-of (:store-of frame)\n               :value val\n               :halted? false))\n      (assoc vm :halted? true, :value val, :store-of nil))))\n\n\n(defn- refuse-continuation!\n  [base entry]\n  (throw (ex-info \"Cannot restore a continuation of another model or image\"\n                  {:reason :foreign-format,\n                   :rule :continuation-format,\n                   :format (:format entry),\n                   :hash (:hash entry),\n                   :image (:image entry),\n                   :expected-format format-tag,\n                   :expected-hash (:hash base),\n                   :images (:images base)})))\n\n\n(defn- check-format!\n  \"Refuse `entry` unless it is this model's payload for a row of the offset\n   table (r6).\"\n  [base entry]\n  (when-not (and (= format-tag (:format entry))\n                 (some #(= (:image entry) (nth % 0)) (:images base)))\n    (refuse-continuation! base entry)))\n\n\n(defn- write-back\n  \"Write `entry`'s registers back and deliver `val` via `:write-result` or\n   `:return-result`. Registers only: `:segment` is kernel state.\"\n  [base entry val]\n  (if (= :return-result (:resume-mode entry))\n    (return-transition (assoc base\n                              :pc (:pc entry)\n                              :frames (:frames entry)\n                              :continuation (:continuation entry)\n                              :store-of (:store-of entry)\n                              :halted? false)\n                       val)\n    (let [pc (:pc entry)\n          body (body-of-pc (:segment base) pc)\n          reg-count (:registers body)\n          dest (:dest entry)\n          restored-regs\n          (reduce (fn [acc [r v]] (assoc acc r v))\n                  (vec (repeat reg-count nil))\n                  (:regs entry))\n          final-regs (if (some? dest)\n                       (assoc restored-regs dest val)\n                       restored-regs)]\n      (assoc base\n             :pc pc\n             :frames (:frames entry)\n             :registers final-regs\n             :continuation (:continuation entry)\n             :store-of (:store-of entry)\n             :value val\n             :halted? false))))\n\n\n(defn register-restore\n  \"The register VM's restore function, `base entry val -> state`\n   (design section 5.2.3). Validates format identity and that the entry's\n   `:image` is a row of the offset table (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3,\n   r6; `:hash` is never a restore key, since it changes at every\n   `attach-image`), checks that the payload is defect-free via\n   effects/continuation-defect, checks that `val` is plain data, handles\n   the FFI two-step, and delivers `val` via `:write-result` or\n   `:return-result`. The entry restores registers only and never assigns\n   `:segment`: the code space is kernel state.\"\n  [base entry val]\n  (check-format! base entry)\n  (when-let [defect (effects/continuation-defect entry)]\n    (throw (ex-info \"Corrupt or tampered continuation payload\"\n                    defect)))\n  (when-not (vm/machine-data? val)\n    (throw (ex-info \"Resume value must be plain data\"\n                    {:rule :resume-value, :val val})))\n  (if (:request-sent entry)\n    (-> base\n        (update :wait-set (fnil conj [])\n                (ffi/response-wait-entry entry (:call-id entry)))\n        (assoc :value :yin/blocked\n               :blocked? true\n               :halted? false))\n    (let [call-id (:call-id entry)\n          base (if call-id (update base :parked dissoc call-id) base)\n          val (if call-id (ffi/call-result val call-id) val)]\n      (write-back base entry val))))\n","numLines":120,"startLine":400,"totalLines":964}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012GxWwnfgD8pYuFceU1RBf3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
