{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FikXEa6mKS5fcV2PmvEB6J","type":"tool_result","content":"1416\t;; Phase 6c: the cross-engine lanes (§5.3, §5.4 laws 4 and 5, §8.3 10-12)\n1417\t;; =============================================================================\n1418\t\n1419\t(def link-rows\n1420\t  \"Rows the de Bruijn lanes do not carry (§5.3, the shared fragment): a\n1421\t   de Bruijn kernel links a native image while module responses carry A,\n1422\t   and §4 defines no layout for install children (canonical-task refuses\n1423\t   :installs). The reference lane runs the whole matrix; these lanes are\n1424\t   removed with their kernels at phase 8.\"\n1425\t  #{7 8 9 10 11 12 17})\n1426\t\n1427\t\n1428\t(def lane-rows\n1429\t  \"The wrapped rows every lane executes: 15 of §5.2's 22.\"\n1430\t  (filterv #(not (contains? link-rows (first %))) rows))\n1431\t\n1432\t\n1433\t(defn lane-cases\n1434\t  \"§5.3's shared fragment: 15 lane rows x 4 segments, plus row 20 once:\n1435\t   [row segment expected build].\"\n1436\t  []\n1437\t  (filterv #(not (contains? link-rows (first %))) (matrix-cases)))\n1438\t\n1439\t\n1440\t(defn on-lane\n1441\t  [lane build]\n1442\t  (binding [*lane* lane] (build)))\n1443\t\n1444\t\n1445\t(defn lane-lift\n1446\t  \"The lift of §7.1 on m's own lane.\"\n1447\t  [m serve!]\n1448\t  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n1449\t    (rows/lift-task m serve! (lift-opts))\n1450\t    (layout/lift-task m (kernel-space m) (on-lane :semantic-register machine) serve! (lift-opts))))\n1451\t\n1452\t\n1453\t(defn lane-lower\n1454\t  \"The lower of §7.2 into a fresh receiver on lane, of composition opts.\"\n1455\t  [lane opts wire attach!]\n1456\t  (let [scratch (on-lane :semantic-register #(machine opts))]\n1457\t    (if (= :semantic-register lane)\n1458\t      (rows/lower-task scratch wire attach!)\n1459\t      (layout/lower-task scratch (on-lane lane #(machine opts)) wire attach!))))\n1460\t\n1461\t\n1462\t(defn injective\n1463\t  \"names, refusing when two identities share a logical name (§5.5).\"\n1464\t  [names]\n1465\t  (when-not (= (count names) (count (distinct (vals names))))\n1466\t    (throw (ex-info \"The correspondence is not injective\" {:law-4 :injective :names names})))\n1467\t  names)\n1468\t\n1469\t\n1470\t(defn logical-names\n1471\t  \"§5.5's explicit correspondence: each served identity to the resource\n1472\t   key the lifted machine holds that handle under. The fixture builds the\n1473\t   same program on every lane, so one key names one logical stream.\"\n1474\t  [m peer]\n1475\t  (injective\n1476\t    (into {} (map (fn [[id e]]\n1477\t                    [id (or (some (fn [[k h]] (when (identical? h (:handle e)) k)) (:resources m))\n1478\t                            (throw (ex-info \"A served handle the machine does not hold\" {:id id})))]))\n1479\t          @(:table peer))))\n1480\t\n1481\t\n1482\t(defn ring-names\n1483\t  \"{stream identity -> resource key} over every stream m holds.\"\n1484\t  [m]\n1485\t  (injective\n1486\t    (into {} (keep (fn [[k h]]\n1487\t                     (when (satisfies? stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor h)\n1488\t                       [(:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor h)) k])))\n1489\t          (:resources m))))\n1490\t\n1491\t\n1492\t(defn logical-positions\n1493\t  \"The task with each cursor position's embedded stream identity renamed\n1494\t   to its logical name. A ring buffer cursor carries its stream's\n1495\t   identity, which §5.5's marker substitution does not reach, so the\n1496\t   cross-lane comparison renames only that field, under the same fixture\n1497\t   correspondence; every other field, the offset included, is kept.\"\n1498\t  [task m]\n1499\t  (let [names (ring-names m)\n1500\t        k :dao.stream.ringbuffer/identity]\n1501\t    (replace-nodes task #(= :cursor-cell-body (:kind %))\n1502\t                   (fn [n]\n1503\t                     (update-in n [:slots 1]\n1504\t                                (fn [p]\n1505\t                                  (if (and (map? p) (contains? names (get p k)))\n1506\t                                    (assoc p k (get names (get p k)))\n1507\t                                    p)))))))\n1508\t\n1509\t\n1510\t(defn rename-identities\n1511\t  \"x with every :dao.stream/identity value that names maps renamed.\"\n1512\t  [x names]\n1513\t  (cond\n1514\t    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]]\n1515\t                             [k (if (and (= :dao.stream/identity k) (contains? names v))\n1516\t                                  (get names v)\n1517\t                                  (rename-identities v names))]))\n1518\t                   x)\n1519\t    (vector? x) (mapv #(rename-identities % names) x)\n1520\t    :else x))\n1521\t\n1522\t\n1523\t(defn logical-descriptors\n1524\t  \"§5.5: {logical name -> stream descriptor, identities renamed} over every\n1525\t   stream m holds. canonical-under erases a marker's descriptor, so the\n1526\t   lanes' descriptors are shown equivalent on these, separately.\"\n1527\t  [m]\n1528\t  (let [names (ring-names m)]\n1529\t    (into {} (keep (fn [[k h]]\n1530\t                     (when (satisfies? stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor h)\n1531\t                       [k (rename-identities (stream/descriptor h) names)])))\n1532\t          (:resources m))))\n1533\t\n1534\t\n1535\t(defn descriptors-equivalent?"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7716a8d-bcb9-4b49-9ad0-ed6a5daed388","uuid":"e601ae8b-96ec-4549-9170-e4e8f51ad885","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:48:07.803Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc","content":";; Phase 6c: the cross-engine lanes (§5.3, §5.4 laws 4 and 5, §8.3 10-12)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def link-rows\n  \"Rows the de Bruijn lanes do not carry (§5.3, the shared fragment): a\n   de Bruijn kernel links a native image while module responses carry A,\n   and §4 defines no layout for install children (canonical-task refuses\n   :installs). The reference lane runs the whole matrix; these lanes are\n   removed with their kernels at phase 8.\"\n  #{7 8 9 10 11 12 17})\n\n\n(def lane-rows\n  \"The wrapped rows every lane executes: 15 of §5.2's 22.\"\n  (filterv #(not (contains? link-rows (first %))) rows))\n\n\n(defn lane-cases\n  \"§5.3's shared fragment: 15 lane rows x 4 segments, plus row 20 once:\n   [row segment expected build].\"\n  []\n  (filterv #(not (contains? link-rows (first %))) (matrix-cases)))\n\n\n(defn on-lane\n  [lane build]\n  (binding [*lane* lane] (build)))\n\n\n(defn lane-lift\n  \"The lift of §7.1 on m's own lane.\"\n  [m serve!]\n  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n    (rows/lift-task m serve! (lift-opts))\n    (layout/lift-task m (kernel-space m) (on-lane :semantic-register machine) serve! (lift-opts))))\n\n\n(defn lane-lower\n  \"The lower of §7.2 into a fresh receiver on lane, of composition opts.\"\n  [lane opts wire attach!]\n  (let [scratch (on-lane :semantic-register #(machine opts))]\n    (if (= :semantic-register lane)\n      (rows/lower-task scratch wire attach!)\n      (layout/lower-task scratch (on-lane lane #(machine opts)) wire attach!))))\n\n\n(defn injective\n  \"names, refusing when two identities share a logical name (§5.5).\"\n  [names]\n  (when-not (= (count names) (count (distinct (vals names))))\n    (throw (ex-info \"The correspondence is not injective\" {:law-4 :injective :names names})))\n  names)\n\n\n(defn logical-names\n  \"§5.5's explicit correspondence: each served identity to the resource\n   key the lifted machine holds that handle under. The fixture builds the\n   same program on every lane, so one key names one logical stream.\"\n  [m peer]\n  (injective\n    (into {} (map (fn [[id e]]\n                    [id (or (some (fn [[k h]] (when (identical? h (:handle e)) k)) (:resources m))\n                            (throw (ex-info \"A served handle the machine does not hold\" {:id id})))]))\n          @(:table peer))))\n\n\n(defn ring-names\n  \"{stream identity -> resource key} over every stream m holds.\"\n  [m]\n  (injective\n    (into {} (keep (fn [[k h]]\n                     (when (satisfies? stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor h)\n                       [(:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor h)) k])))\n          (:resources m))))\n\n\n(defn logical-positions\n  \"The task with each cursor position's embedded stream identity renamed\n   to its logical name. A ring buffer cursor carries its stream's\n   identity, which §5.5's marker substitution does not reach, so the\n   cross-lane comparison renames only that field, under the same fixture\n   correspondence; every other field, the offset included, is kept.\"\n  [task m]\n  (let [names (ring-names m)\n        k :dao.stream.ringbuffer/identity]\n    (replace-nodes task #(= :cursor-cell-body (:kind %))\n                   (fn [n]\n                     (update-in n [:slots 1]\n                                (fn [p]\n                                  (if (and (map? p) (contains? names (get p k)))\n                                    (assoc p k (get names (get p k)))\n                                    p)))))))\n\n\n(defn rename-identities\n  \"x with every :dao.stream/identity value that names maps renamed.\"\n  [x names]\n  (cond\n    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]]\n                             [k (if (and (= :dao.stream/identity k) (contains? names v))\n                                  (get names v)\n                                  (rename-identities v names))]))\n                   x)\n    (vector? x) (mapv #(rename-identities % names) x)\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn logical-descriptors\n  \"§5.5: {logical name -> stream descriptor, identities renamed} over every\n   stream m holds. canonical-under erases a marker's descriptor, so the\n   lanes' descriptors are shown equivalent on these, separately.\"\n  [m]\n  (let [names (ring-names m)]\n    (into {} (keep (fn [[k h]]\n                     (when (satisfies? stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor h)\n                       [k (rename-identities (stream/descriptor h) names)])))\n          (:resources m))))\n\n\n(defn descriptors-equivalent?","numLines":120,"startLine":1416,"totalLines":1931}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FikXEa6mKS5fcV2PmvEB6J","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
