{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016SfgpCNV5DiQqHxm2Cj1fF","type":"tool_result","content":"1795\t(defn spare-register\n1796\t  \"A physical register of the entry's body outside its live set and its\n1797\t   destination that R gives exactly one virtual.\"\n1798\t  [m entry]\n1799\t  (let [sg (val (first (:segments (kernel-space m))))\n1800\t        site (- (:site-pc entry) (layout/offset :register m sg))\n1801\t        body (nth (:phys sg) (code/body-index (:bodies sg) site))\n1802\t        unique (keep (fn [[s xs]] (when (= 1 (count xs)) s)) (group-by body (keys body)))]\n1803\t    (first (remove (conj (set (:live entry)) (:dest entry)) (sort unique)))))\n1804\t\n1805\t\n1806\t(def layout-corpus\n1807\t  \"C, [label ast]: the B0 corpus, the phase-3 corpus, then a tail call in\n1808\t   operand position, whose dead layout syntax reads registers other than\n1809\t   the call's own (phase-5 §6.3's last golden).\"\n1810\t  (conj (into (mapv (fn [[label ast _]] [label ast]) b0/corpus) corpus/programs)\n1811\t        [:tail-operand (corpus/app (corpus/v 'f) (corpus/tail (corpus/app (corpus/v 'g) (corpus/v 'x))) (corpus/v 'y))]))\n1812\t\n1813\t\n1814\t(defn- parking-site?\n1815\t  \"Rule A1: a non-tail parking instruction.\"\n1816\t  [t]\n1817\t  (or (contains? #{:stream-next :stream-put :ffi-call :park :current-continuation} (nth t 0))\n1818\t      (and (= :call (nth t 0)) (not (code/tail-call? t)))))\n1819\t\n1820\t\n1821\t(defn ambiguous-dead-slots\n1822\t  \"[v p s] over C: a reachable parking pc p and a physical slot s of its\n1823\t   body that R gives two or more virtuals, outside live-out*(p)'s image\n1824\t   and p's destination.\"\n1825\t  []\n1826\t  (into []\n1827\t        (mapcat (fn [[_ ast]]\n1828\t                  (let [v (:vector (linearize/project ast))\n1829\t                        sg (segment-of v)\n1830\t                        reach (into #{} (mapcat #(analysis/reachable v (:start %))) (code/body-ranges v))]