{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T7u676DyPJL6y76jUYad5w","type":"tool_result","content":"1405\t                                                 :yin.admit/asserters\n1406\t                                                 :yin.admit/address])))\n1407\t                    received (receive-module state module-name entry)\n1408\t                    received (reduce\n1409\t                               (fn [s [m dep]]\n1410\t                                 (if (some? (module/module-entry\n1411\t                                              (:modules (:modules s)) m))\n1412\t                                   s\n1413\t                                   (receive-module s m (dissoc dep :bindings))))\n1414\t                               received\n1415\t                               (linked-entries (:modules vm)))]\n1416\t                (-> received\n1417\t                    (update :installs dissoc module-name)\n1418\t                    (wake-installed module-name module-name nil))))))))))\n1419\t\n1420\t\n1421\t(defn- advance-install\n1422\t  \"Step the install child of `module-name` in this round, beside every\n1423\t   other task (section 7.3): `running` runs it until it halts or parks.\n1424\t   A parked child stays `parked`; a halted one goes on to `validated`; an\n1425\t   error refuses the install. An error while publishing -- attaching an\n1426\t   origin image, lowering the slice or a store snapshot, or receiving a\n1427\t   dependency -- refuses it too, at phase `:linked`, from the state the\n1428\t   round started with: nothing half-published survives, every waiter is\n1429\t   restored with the refusal, and no throw leaves the round.\n1430\t\n1431\t   Under a custody gate the child is stamped with the root's mode before\n1432\t   it runs; in `:exporting` and `:ended` it does not run.\"\n1433\t  [state module-name]\n1434\t  (let [inst (get-in state [:installs module-name])\n1435\t        mode (vm/gate-mode state)\n