{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KiYAsTAPo8k5qbskEafGb1","type":"tool_result","content":"618\t## 4. Safepoints and the continuation format\n619\t\n620\t### 4.1 The safepoint table (UCF §7.4.1, rewritten)\n621\t\n622\tA safepoint is a transition at which the machine parks. The semantic\n623\tkinds are unchanged; the state columns are new.\n624\t\n625\tEvery wait is one of the two closed states of §2.4 (`act` with\n626\t`{:deliver :rd}` or `tail` with `{:deliver :return}`); an effectful\n627\ttail call raises the `tail` form of whichever row its effect falls in.\n628\t`saved` is `saved(pc+1, rd)` of §2.4.\n629\t\n630\t| Safepoint kind | Raised by | State | Delivery |\n631\t|---|---|---|---|\n632\t| blocked read | `:stream-next rd c` → `blocked` | `act`, pending cursor cell `c` | `rd` ← read value; nil on `end`; `:dao.stream/gap` on gap |\n633\t| blocked write | `:stream-put rd s v` → `full` | `act`, pending retains `W[v]` and the stream | `rd` ← written value on retry `ok` |\n634\t| FFI call, sent | `:ffi-call rd op args` → `ok` | `act`, pending `:ffi` (call id, response cursor cell); in-VM `:reason :next` with `:call-id` | `rd` ← correlated `ok` value; `error` raises; bookkeeping removed |\n635\t| FFI call, retained | `:ffi-call` → `full` | `act`, pending `:ffi-request` (envelope verbatim); in-VM `:reason :put` with `:request-sent` | none at this phase; on append `ok` the entry becomes the sent phase |\n636\t| effectful call, non-tail | `:call rd f args false` whose operator yields a blocking effect | `act`, pending per the effect kind | per the kind's row |\n637\t| effectful call, tail | `:call rd f args true` likewise | `tail`, pending per the effect kind | **through return** against `K` |\n638\t| link request | `:module/require` miss, request in hand | `act` or `tail`, pending `:link-request` | none at this phase; on append `ok` the entry becomes link response |\n639\t| link response | request appended; polling for the correlated response | same state, pending `:link-response` | none at this phase; a matching `ok` makes it install; refusal raises |\n640\t| install | the child runs | same state, pending `:install` + the body's install entry | on `linked`: the module symbol to `rd` or through return; on `refused`: raises |\n641\t| halt | `:halt r`, or `:return r` with empty `K` | — | not resumable; a `:yin.k/result` travels |\n642\t\n643\tTwo cases sit outside the table: an **explicit park** (`:park rd`) is a\n644\t**no-wait safepoint**: it is a migration safepoint like every row\n645\tabove, but it raises no wait entry; its `act` record is the body's\n646\tparked record and a body of kind `:parked` names it by id (UCF §7.4.3\n647\tr5, \"explicit park is the no-wait shape\"). A **reified continuation**\n648\t(`:current-continuation`) is the one thing here that is *not* a\n649\tsafepoint: it is a captured value, never a task state.\n650\tWhole-task quiescence (empty ready queue, UCF §7.4.1) and the existing\n651\trefusal conditions (unsupported observation states, pending close) are\n652\tunchanged.\n653\t\n654\tThe \"effectful call, tail\" row is the one place the rewrite is more\n655\tthan notation: in the stack machine a tail effect's resume value landed\n656\tin `val` and the body's `:return` then delivered it; here the body has\n657\tno activation to resume into, so §2.4's `tail` state routes delivery\n658\tthrough `K`. Write-result and through-return delivery are distinguished\n659\tby the closed `deliver` record.\n660\t\n661\t### 4.2 The UCF frame\n662\t\n663\t`:yin.k/frame` (UCF §7.4.1) becomes, for the semantic profile:\n664\t\n665\t```clojure\n666\t;; an act state (write-result delivery)\n667\t{:yin.k/state    :act\n668\t :yin.k/segment  A\n669\t :yin.k/pc       n                       ; the resume pc, already pc+1\n670\t :yin.k/reason   …                       ; unchanged\n671\t :yin.k/window   {r (encoded) …}         ; saved(pc, rd), sorted by r\n672\t :yin.k/deliver  {:yin.k/deliver :rd :yin.k/rd r}\n673\t :yin.k/env      {sym encoded …}         ; E, unchanged\n674\t :yin.k/k        [ {:yin.k/frame-type :return\n675\t                    :yin.k/segment A :yin.k/pc n\n676\t                    :yin.k/env {…} :yin.k/window {…} :yin.k/rd r} … ]\n677\t :yin.k/pending  {…}}                    ; unchanged, §7.4.3\n678\t\n679\t;; a tail state (through-return delivery)\n680\t{:yin.k/state    :tail\n681\t :yin.k/segment  A :yin.k/site n         ; the tail call site, for provenance only\n682\t :yin.k/reason   …\n683\t :yin.k/deliver  {:yin.k/deliver :return}\n684\t :yin.k/k        [ … ]                   ; the frames delivery will pop\n685\t :yin.k/pending  {…}}\n686\t```\n687\t\n688\t`:yin.k/val`, `:yin.k/stack` and `:stack-base` are gone. The window's\n689\t**membership is validated**, not trusted: the receiver recomputes\n690\t`saved(pc, rd)` from A (§8.1) and refuses a window with a register\n691\toutside it (`:window-extra`), missing from it (`:window-missing`), or\n692\tcontaining the delivery destination (`:window-self`). Those three are\n693\tthe membership diagnostics; the full frame validator also checks\n694\trepresentation (integer ids, sorted unique keys), body scope (every\n695\tregister of the window belongs to the body `pc` is in), site/pc pairing\n696\t(`pc` is a safepoint successor of the right kind for `reason`;\n697\t`site` is a tail call), destination equality (`rd` is the `rd` of the\n698\tinstruction at `pc−1`), delivery mode (`:act` carries `:rd`, `:tail`\n699\tcarries `:return` and no window or env), return-frame sites (each\n700\t`:return` frame's `pc` follows a non-tail call whose `rd` it names, and\n701\tits window is `saved(pc, rd)` of that body), `K` structure (frames\n702\tinnermost last, each well-formed), and pending compatibility with\n703\t`reason`. Two captures of equal state therefore encode identically, and\n704\tdead values never travel.\n705\t\n706\tThe validator is the pure function `(defect frame code context task)`\n707\tof `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §3: `task` is decoded\n708\ttask context (the parked key, the live FFI call ids, the free\n709\tenvironment), never an engine; its rules are ordered, structural checks\n710\tfirst, current-window rules on `act` only, return windows separately,\n711\tand every `E` is checked to agree with the task's free environment off\n712\tthe lexical names; it runs after canonical numbering, as the carrier\n713\torders it.\n714\t\n715\tThe row carrier (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md` §5.2) changes\n716\taccordingly: the frame rows are `:act [segment-A pc env-cref window-cref\n717\tk-cref rd]` and `:tail [segment-A site k-cref]`, the kind being the\n718\tdelivery discriminant, so `deliver` is not a slot; `:window` is a keyed\n719\trow `[r₁ V₁ r₂ V₂ …]` sorted by `r` in which a nil-valued register is a\n720\tpresent `[:lit nil]`; `:kframe` is `[segment-A pc env-cref window-cref\n721\trd]`; `:stack` and `stack-base` are removed; the root gains `free-env`,\n722\tthe task's initial free environment (continuation design §2, §6.3).\n723\tThat amendment is applied to the carrier draft with this design's\n724\tphase 6 (§10; `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §10.3).\n725\t\n726\t### 4.3 Foreign engines (UCF §7.4.2)\n727\t\n728\tA foreign engine's static safepoint map keeps `:yin.safepoint/segment`,\n729\t`:yin.safepoint/pc` and `:yin.safepoint/engine`, replaces\n730\t`:stack-effect` with the per-pc **def and use sets** and `L(pc)` derived\n731\tfrom A (§8.1), and keeps `:yin.safepoint/layout` as a map from physical\n732\tlocation to virtual register. The reconstruction obligation is: for an\n733\t`act` state, produce the segment `A` and resume `pc`, every register in\n734\t`saved(pc, rd) = L(pc) − {rd}` (never the not-yet-produced\n735\tdestination), `E`, `K` with each frame's validated window and `rd`, the\n736\tdelivery record, the pending state, and the captured store context; for\n737\ta `tail` state, produce the segment and the tail `site`, `K` with its"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7716a8d-bcb9-4b49-9ad0-ed6a5daed388","uuid":"137f57e4-f2e8-40d0-ae0a-07ca0016472b","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:50:56.104Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md","content":"## 4. Safepoints and the continuation format\n\n### 4.1 The safepoint table (UCF §7.4.1, rewritten)\n\nA safepoint is a transition at which the machine parks. The semantic\nkinds are unchanged; the state columns are new.\n\nEvery wait is one of the two closed states of §2.4 (`act` with\n`{:deliver :rd}` or `tail` with `{:deliver :return}`); an effectful\ntail call raises the `tail` form of whichever row its effect falls in.\n`saved` is `saved(pc+1, rd)` of §2.4.\n\n| Safepoint kind | Raised by | State | Delivery |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| blocked read | `:stream-next rd c` → `blocked` | `act`, pending cursor cell `c` | `rd` ← read value; nil on `end`; `:dao.stream/gap` on gap |\n| blocked write | `:stream-put rd s v` → `full` | `act`, pending retains `W[v]` and the stream | `rd` ← written value on retry `ok` |\n| FFI call, sent | `:ffi-call rd op args` → `ok` | `act`, pending `:ffi` (call id, response cursor cell); in-VM `:reason :next` with `:call-id` | `rd` ← correlated `ok` value; `error` raises; bookkeeping removed |\n| FFI call, retained | `:ffi-call` → `full` | `act`, pending `:ffi-request` (envelope verbatim); in-VM `:reason :put` with `:request-sent` | none at this phase; on append `ok` the entry becomes the sent phase |\n| effectful call, non-tail | `:call rd f args false` whose operator yields a blocking effect | `act`, pending per the effect kind | per the kind's row |\n| effectful call, tail | `:call rd f args true` likewise | `tail`, pending per the effect kind | **through return** against `K` |\n| link request | `:module/require` miss, request in hand | `act` or `tail`, pending `:link-request` | none at this phase; on append `ok` the entry becomes link response |\n| link response | request appended; polling for the correlated response | same state, pending `:link-response` | none at this phase; a matching `ok` makes it install; refusal raises |\n| install | the child runs | same state, pending `:install` + the body's install entry | on `linked`: the module symbol to `rd` or through return; on `refused`: raises |\n| halt | `:halt r`, or `:return r` with empty `K` | — | not resumable; a `:yin.k/result` travels |\n\nTwo cases sit outside the table: an **explicit park** (`:park rd`) is a\n**no-wait safepoint**: it is a migration safepoint like every row\nabove, but it raises no wait entry; its `act` record is the body's\nparked record and a body of kind `:parked` names it by id (UCF §7.4.3\nr5, \"explicit park is the no-wait shape\"). A **reified continuation**\n(`:current-continuation`) is the one thing here that is *not* a\nsafepoint: it is a captured value, never a task state.\nWhole-task quiescence (empty ready queue, UCF §7.4.1) and the existing\nrefusal conditions (unsupported observation states, pending close) are\nunchanged.\n\nThe \"effectful call, tail\" row is the one place the rewrite is more\nthan notation: in the stack machine a tail effect's resume value landed\nin `val` and the body's `:return` then delivered it; here the body has\nno activation to resume into, so §2.4's `tail` state routes delivery\nthrough `K`. Write-result and through-return delivery are distinguished\nby the closed `deliver` record.\n\n### 4.2 The UCF frame\n\n`:yin.k/frame` (UCF §7.4.1) becomes, for the semantic profile:\n\n```clojure\n;; an act state (write-result delivery)\n{:yin.k/state    :act\n :yin.k/segment  A\n :yin.k/pc       n                       ; the resume pc, already pc+1\n :yin.k/reason   …                       ; unchanged\n :yin.k/window   {r (encoded) …}         ; saved(pc, rd), sorted by r\n :yin.k/deliver  {:yin.k/deliver :rd :yin.k/rd r}\n :yin.k/env      {sym encoded …}         ; E, unchanged\n :yin.k/k        [ {:yin.k/frame-type :return\n                    :yin.k/segment A :yin.k/pc n\n                    :yin.k/env {…} :yin.k/window {…} :yin.k/rd r} … ]\n :yin.k/pending  {…}}                    ; unchanged, §7.4.3\n\n;; a tail state (through-return delivery)\n{:yin.k/state    :tail\n :yin.k/segment  A :yin.k/site n         ; the tail call site, for provenance only\n :yin.k/reason   …\n :yin.k/deliver  {:yin.k/deliver :return}\n :yin.k/k        [ … ]                   ; the frames delivery will pop\n :yin.k/pending  {…}}\n```\n\n`:yin.k/val`, `:yin.k/stack` and `:stack-base` are gone. The window's\n**membership is validated**, not trusted: the receiver recomputes\n`saved(pc, rd)` from A (§8.1) and refuses a window with a register\noutside it (`:window-extra`), missing from it (`:window-missing`), or\ncontaining the delivery destination (`:window-self`). Those three are\nthe membership diagnostics; the full frame validator also checks\nrepresentation (integer ids, sorted unique keys), body scope (every\nregister of the window belongs to the body `pc` is in), site/pc pairing\n(`pc` is a safepoint successor of the right kind for `reason`;\n`site` is a tail call), destination equality (`rd` is the `rd` of the\ninstruction at `pc−1`), delivery mode (`:act` carries `:rd`, `:tail`\ncarries `:return` and no window or env), return-frame sites (each\n`:return` frame's `pc` follows a non-tail call whose `rd` it names, and\nits window is `saved(pc, rd)` of that body), `K` structure (frames\ninnermost last, each well-formed), and pending compatibility with\n`reason`. Two captures of equal state therefore encode identically, and\ndead values never travel.\n\nThe validator is the pure function `(defect frame code context task)`\nof `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §3: `task` is decoded\ntask context (the parked key, the live FFI call ids, the free\nenvironment), never an engine; its rules are ordered, structural checks\nfirst, current-window rules on `act` only, return windows separately,\nand every `E` is checked to agree with the task's free environment off\nthe lexical names; it runs after canonical numbering, as the carrier\norders it.\n\nThe row carrier (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md` §5.2) changes\naccordingly: the frame rows are `:act [segment-A pc env-cref window-cref\nk-cref rd]` and `:tail [segment-A site k-cref]`, the kind being the\ndelivery discriminant, so `deliver` is not a slot; `:window` is a keyed\nrow `[r₁ V₁ r₂ V₂ …]` sorted by `r` in which a nil-valued register is a\npresent `[:lit nil]`; `:kframe` is `[segment-A pc env-cref window-cref\nrd]`; `:stack` and `stack-base` are removed; the root gains `free-env`,\nthe task's initial free environment (continuation design §2, §6.3).\nThat amendment is applied to the carrier draft with this design's\nphase 6 (§10; `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §10.3).\n\n### 4.3 Foreign engines (UCF §7.4.2)\n\nA foreign engine's static safepoint map keeps `:yin.safepoint/segment`,\n`:yin.safepoint/pc` and `:yin.safepoint/engine`, replaces\n`:stack-effect` with the per-pc **def and use sets** and `L(pc)` derived\nfrom A (§8.1), and keeps `:yin.safepoint/layout` as a map from physical\nlocation to virtual register. The reconstruction obligation is: for an\n`act` state, produce the segment `A` and resume `pc`, every register in\n`saved(pc, rd) = L(pc) − {rd}` (never the not-yet-produced\ndestination), `E`, `K` with each frame's validated window and `rd`, the\ndelivery record, the pending state, and the captured store context; for\na `tail` state, produce the segment and the tail `site`, `K` with its","numLines":120,"startLine":618,"totalLines":1155}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KiYAsTAPo8k5qbskEafGb1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
