{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NPJsj26bpvSvWRSCdzburD","type":"tool_result","content":"1019\t## 10. Migration\n1020\t\n1021\tEight phases, each gated; the old evaluator survives only as an oracle\n1022\tuntil phase 8.\n1023\t\n1024\t1. **Identity.** Amend the A-only identity contracts. **Complete**\n1025\t   (merged to master 2026-10-10, `2daa17fb`). Independent of this VM.\n1026\t2. **Freeze.** This document's §3 (grammar, minting), §4 (windows,\n1027\t   delivery, safepoint table), §6 (stamps), §3.4 (rejection rules) are\n1028\t   reviewed and frozen. Gate: Architect sign-off on the frozen text.\n1029\t3. **Linearizer, validator, static analysis.** `project` per §3.3, the\n1030\t   loader rules of §3.4 (both load paths), **and the §8.1 analysis\n1031\t   (def, use, `L`, `saved`)**, which the phase-4 evaluator needs for\n1032\t   every call save and capture and so cannot wait for phase 5. Gate:\n1033\t   deterministic vectors across JVM/Node/Dart on the corpus (the same\n1034\t   inline goldens and pinned addresses on all three); malformed-input\n1035\t   refusal rows for every rule including item 13, on the direct vector;\n1036\t   both AST projection lanes and the direct vector load through the one\n1037\t   validator to equal images (§3.4, direct-vector form; the\n1038\t   vector→datoms equivalence is retired); `L` agrees with an\n1039\t   independent reference implementation on the corpus. The image\n1040\t   `load-vector` returns is `{:vector :address :bodies [{:start :end\n1041\t   :owner :registers}]}` with `:end` **exclusive**; phase 4 computes\n1042\t   `analysis` once per admitted image as engine-local derived data, and\n1043\t   neither parsed trees nor saved sets enter canonical content.\n1044\t   *(Met 2026-10-10, commit 7a010962 on `srvm-phase3`; Architect\n1045\t   review `collab/1791530000000-architect-srvm-phase3-review.*`.)*\n1046\t4. **Evaluator.** `yin.vm.semantic-register` beside `yin.vm.semantic`.\n1047\t   During coexistence the evaluator links under the interim format\n1048\t   `:yin.semantic-register/code`, contract `\"v4\"`; phase 5 supplies its\n1049\t   production linker format record (the dependency-closure scanners over\n1050\t   the new table), and phase 8 retires it in favour of\n1051\t   `:yin.semantic/code` `\"v4\"`.\n1052\t   Gate: walker parity on the full B0 corpus (values, store, effects,\n1053\t   halting) under the §2.5 correspondence; Rule R rows; effects,\n1054\t   non-tail and tail recursion, pure and effectful tail completion,\n1055\t   continuation invocation (including abortive invoke and ownership\n1056\t   refusal), park/resume, gensym, module `store-of`, FFI\n1057\t   retained-request and response phases.\n1058\t5. **Derivations.** §8.2-8.3 implemented; the lexical-address law\n1059\t   (`addresses(H) = addresses(R) = addresses(resolve(A))`) and\n1060\t   behavioural parity of all three kernels on the corpus; the\n1061\t   execution oracle, validators, goldens and determinism checks of §8.4\n1062\t   green on three hosts, the slow C4 rows actually run; **the\n1063\t   dependency-closure scanners (UCF §7.6.1) reimplemented over the\n1064\t   new table agree with the old ones and with the tree-side oracles on\n1065\t   the B0 corpus, the register corpus and the C4 linked-prelude modules\n1066\t   by name**, under three obligations (derivations design §7.3): (i)\n1067\t   unordered agreement, old = new = the tree scanners and queries, on\n1068\t   free-name sets, the multiset of free-name occurrences as\n1069\t   `[name in-body?]`, the multiset of definitions as `[name conditional?]`,\n1070\t   and the store-key, FFI-op, parked-id and effect-kind sets (positions\n1071\t   excluded since the layouts differ; the tree scanners order by\n1072\t   structural path and are compared unordered); (ii) ordered agreement,\n1073\t   old = new = an independent emission-order tree oracle (main sequence\n1074\t   then bodies FIFO; a definition visits only its value operand), on the\n1075\t   occurrence and definition sequences and on the application-site count\n1076\t   (definition applications excluded, FFI sites included); (iii) join\n1077\t   agreement through `linker/verify`, old = new on the **complete\n1078\t   normalised outcome**: a success with its retained obligations as\n1079\t   `[name in-body?]` in order, or a refusal with its reason and name\n1080\t   (`:use-before-definition` included, exercised by a row that must\n1081\t   refuse on both sides). The old scanners' answers, normalised joins\n1082\t   included, are pinned as goldens before cutover deletes them, since the\n1083\t   C4 track's module declarations are built against those answers; the\n1084\t   C4 gate is read-only and compares declarations against the discharged\n1085\t   external-name set (module-defined keys and `yin/def` removed,\n1086\t   requirement-covered names removed), not raw free names.\n1087\t6. **Continuation format.** §4.2 frames and both state shapes, the\n1088\t   full frame validator, the safepoint harness of §4.1 (bidirectional\n1089\t   lift/lower rows for every kind and both delivery modes, pending\n1090\t   waits, nested and reified captures, module contexts, refusals); the\n1091\t   row carrier amended to body version 3 with one profile,\n1092\t   `{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`, carrying canonical\n1093\t   vectors by A, `:yin.k/trees` and the task's free environment, never\n1094\t   a native image (continuation design §2, §6). Gate: UCF §7.11's\n1095\t   harness green **for every engine intended to reconstruct canonical\n1096\t   frames** (the semantic kernel, the stack and register kernels through\n1097\t   their layouts, the stack kernel with its tail-completion seam; the\n1098\t   walker is excluded), not the semantic profile alone.\n1099\t7. **Stage D/E rerun.** Handoff, fencing, custody, durability,\n1100\t   crash-cut and cross-process acceptance over the new transport, three\n1101\t   hosts.\n1102\t8. **Cutover.** Delete `yin.vm.semantic` (old), rename\n1103\t   `yin.vm.semantic-register` to `yin.vm.semantic`, remove the old H/R\n1104\t   request paths and the `raise` dependency, remove the `:dim/lift-to`\n1105\t   row from both de Bruijn descriptors without a version bump and\n1106\t   regenerate the descriptor hashes and every pinned H and R\n1107\t   (derivations design §8.1-8.2); delete `yin.vm.debruijn-resolve`,\n1108\t   `yin.vm.debruijn-linearize`, `yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile` and\n1109\t   their tests only after the replacement coverage of §8.4 is green and\n1110\t   the descriptor-hash golden has moved to a surviving namespace; switch\n1111\t   `linker/relowered`, `publish-closure!` and the REPL to the A-derived\n1112\t   lowerings (derivations design §8.3); regenerate the manifests'\n1113\t   derivation records as `A → H`, `A → R` and the format index in its\n1114\t   final shape `{format storage-address}` (derivations design §7.6,\n1115\t   §8.1); run the C4 suite over the newly published images as the\n1116\t   install-child gate (derivations design §6.1.4 (c)); finalize\n1117\t   documentation. No compatibility shim.\n1118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7716a8d-bcb9-4b49-9ad0-ed6a5daed388","uuid":"9d06d62f-231e-473a-b62c-167a3817a859","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:51:24.742Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md","content":"## 10. Migration\n\nEight phases, each gated; the old evaluator survives only as an oracle\nuntil phase 8.\n\n1. **Identity.** Amend the A-only identity contracts. **Complete**\n   (merged to master 2026-10-10, `2daa17fb`). Independent of this VM.\n2. **Freeze.** This document's §3 (grammar, minting), §4 (windows,\n   delivery, safepoint table), §6 (stamps), §3.4 (rejection rules) are\n   reviewed and frozen. Gate: Architect sign-off on the frozen text.\n3. **Linearizer, validator, static analysis.** `project` per §3.3, the\n   loader rules of §3.4 (both load paths), **and the §8.1 analysis\n   (def, use, `L`, `saved`)**, which the phase-4 evaluator needs for\n   every call save and capture and so cannot wait for phase 5. Gate:\n   deterministic vectors across JVM/Node/Dart on the corpus (the same\n   inline goldens and pinned addresses on all three); malformed-input\n   refusal rows for every rule including item 13, on the direct vector;\n   both AST projection lanes and the direct vector load through the one\n   validator to equal images (§3.4, direct-vector form; the\n   vector→datoms equivalence is retired); `L` agrees with an\n   independent reference implementation on the corpus. The image\n   `load-vector` returns is `{:vector :address :bodies [{:start :end\n   :owner :registers}]}` with `:end` **exclusive**; phase 4 computes\n   `analysis` once per admitted image as engine-local derived data, and\n   neither parsed trees nor saved sets enter canonical content.\n   *(Met 2026-10-10, commit 7a010962 on `srvm-phase3`; Architect\n   review `collab/1791530000000-architect-srvm-phase3-review.*`.)*\n4. **Evaluator.** `yin.vm.semantic-register` beside `yin.vm.semantic`.\n   During coexistence the evaluator links under the interim format\n   `:yin.semantic-register/code`, contract `\"v4\"`; phase 5 supplies its\n   production linker format record (the dependency-closure scanners over\n   the new table), and phase 8 retires it in favour of\n   `:yin.semantic/code` `\"v4\"`.\n   Gate: walker parity on the full B0 corpus (values, store, effects,\n   halting) under the §2.5 correspondence; Rule R rows; effects,\n   non-tail and tail recursion, pure and effectful tail completion,\n   continuation invocation (including abortive invoke and ownership\n   refusal), park/resume, gensym, module `store-of`, FFI\n   retained-request and response phases.\n5. **Derivations.** §8.2-8.3 implemented; the lexical-address law\n   (`addresses(H) = addresses(R) = addresses(resolve(A))`) and\n   behavioural parity of all three kernels on the corpus; the\n   execution oracle, validators, goldens and determinism checks of §8.4\n   green on three hosts, the slow C4 rows actually run; **the\n   dependency-closure scanners (UCF §7.6.1) reimplemented over the\n   new table agree with the old ones and with the tree-side oracles on\n   the B0 corpus, the register corpus and the C4 linked-prelude modules\n   by name**, under three obligations (derivations design §7.3): (i)\n   unordered agreement, old = new = the tree scanners and queries, on\n   free-name sets, the multiset of free-name occurrences as\n   `[name in-body?]`, the multiset of definitions as `[name conditional?]`,\n   and the store-key, FFI-op, parked-id and effect-kind sets (positions\n   excluded since the layouts differ; the tree scanners order by\n   structural path and are compared unordered); (ii) ordered agreement,\n   old = new = an independent emission-order tree oracle (main sequence\n   then bodies FIFO; a definition visits only its value operand), on the\n   occurrence and definition sequences and on the application-site count\n   (definition applications excluded, FFI sites included); (iii) join\n   agreement through `linker/verify`, old = new on the **complete\n   normalised outcome**: a success with its retained obligations as\n   `[name in-body?]` in order, or a refusal with its reason and name\n   (`:use-before-definition` included, exercised by a row that must\n   refuse on both sides). The old scanners' answers, normalised joins\n   included, are pinned as goldens before cutover deletes them, since the\n   C4 track's module declarations are built against those answers; the\n   C4 gate is read-only and compares declarations against the discharged\n   external-name set (module-defined keys and `yin/def` removed,\n   requirement-covered names removed), not raw free names.\n6. **Continuation format.** §4.2 frames and both state shapes, the\n   full frame validator, the safepoint harness of §4.1 (bidirectional\n   lift/lower rows for every kind and both delivery modes, pending\n   waits, nested and reified captures, module contexts, refusals); the\n   row carrier amended to body version 3 with one profile,\n   `{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`, carrying canonical\n   vectors by A, `:yin.k/trees` and the task's free environment, never\n   a native image (continuation design §2, §6). Gate: UCF §7.11's\n   harness green **for every engine intended to reconstruct canonical\n   frames** (the semantic kernel, the stack and register kernels through\n   their layouts, the stack kernel with its tail-completion seam; the\n   walker is excluded), not the semantic profile alone.\n7. **Stage D/E rerun.** Handoff, fencing, custody, durability,\n   crash-cut and cross-process acceptance over the new transport, three\n   hosts.\n8. **Cutover.** Delete `yin.vm.semantic` (old), rename\n   `yin.vm.semantic-register` to `yin.vm.semantic`, remove the old H/R\n   request paths and the `raise` dependency, remove the `:dim/lift-to`\n   row from both de Bruijn descriptors without a version bump and\n   regenerate the descriptor hashes and every pinned H and R\n   (derivations design §8.1-8.2); delete `yin.vm.debruijn-resolve`,\n   `yin.vm.debruijn-linearize`, `yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile` and\n   their tests only after the replacement coverage of §8.4 is green and\n   the descriptor-hash golden has moved to a surviving namespace; switch\n   `linker/relowered`, `publish-closure!` and the REPL to the A-derived\n   lowerings (derivations design §8.3); regenerate the manifests'\n   derivation records as `A → H`, `A → R` and the format index in its\n   final shape `{format storage-address}` (derivations design §7.6,\n   §8.1); run the C4 suite over the newly published images as the\n   install-child gate (derivations design §6.1.4 (c)); finalize\n   documentation. No compatibility shim.\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1019,"totalLines":1155}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NPJsj26bpvSvWRSCdzburD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0165pMDkrW1gCyHxQ2rR4HFi","type":"tool_result","content":"490\t      (fail \"Gate is closed: no observation\"\n491\t            {:yin.k/gate mode, :effect (:effect effect)}))\n492\t    mode))\n493\t\n494\t\n495\t(defn- observe-put\n496\t  \"Observe half of `:stream/put`: the append, as its outcome.\"\n497\t  [state stream-id val]\n498\t  (stream/append! (get (:resources state) stream-id) val))\n499\t\n500\t\n501\t(defn- apply-put-outcome\n502\t  \"Apply half of `:stream/put`: an append outcome to the effect's answer.\"\n503\t  [state stream-id val result]\n504\t  (let [o (outcome result)]\n505\t    (case o\n506\t      :dao.stream/ok {:value val, :state state}\n507\t      :dao.stream/full {:park true, :stream-id stream-id, :state state}\n508\t      (:dao.stream/closed\n509\t        :dao.stream/invalid-value\n510\t        :dao.stream/transport-error)\n511\t      (fail \"Stream append failed\" {:outcome o, :stream-id stream-id})\n512\t      {:state state,\n513\t       :value {:status :refused, :outcome o, :stream-id stream-id}})))\n514\t\n515\t\n516\t(defn handle-put\n517\t  \"Handle :stream/put. Total over the six append outcomes, once the\n518\t   reference verifies.\n519\t   Returns {:value v :state s} on success, {:park true :stream-id id :state s}\n520\t   on `full`. `closed`, `invalid-value` and `transport-error` are errors\n521\t   that name their outcome, as v1's throw on a closed stream did.\n522\t   `refused`, and any outcome outside this contract version, is not a\n523\t   throw: the effect's value is the shaped refusal\n524\t   {:status :refused, :outcome o, :stream-id id} -- data the program\n525\t   reads, the way `poll-link-response` answers a refused link.\n526\t\n527\t   Under the `:running` gate nothing is observed: the put parks as it\n528\t   would on `full`.\"\n529\t  [state effect]\n530\t  (let [stream-id (check-ref! state :stream/put :stream-ref (:stream effect))\n531\t        val (:val effect)]\n532\t    (if (= :running (gate-refuse! state effect))\n533\t      {:park true, :stream-id stream-id, :state state}\n534\t      (apply-put-outcome state stream-id val"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7716a8d-bcb9-4b49-9ad0-ed6a5daed388","uuid":"4edd665e-0cb2-493f-95e9-c1338aa2bb19","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:51:24.745Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7plan/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc","content":"      (fail \"Gate is closed: no observation\"\n            {:yin.k/gate mode, :effect (:effect effect)}))\n    mode))\n\n\n(defn- observe-put\n  \"Observe half of `:stream/put`: the append, as its outcome.\"\n  [state stream-id val]\n  (stream/append! (get (:resources state) stream-id) val))\n\n\n(defn- apply-put-outcome\n  \"Apply half of `:stream/put`: an append outcome to the effect's answer.\"\n  [state stream-id val result]\n  (let [o (outcome result)]\n    (case o\n      :dao.stream/ok {:value val, :state state}\n      :dao.stream/full {:park true, :stream-id stream-id, :state state}\n      (:dao.stream/closed\n        :dao.stream/invalid-value\n        :dao.stream/transport-error)\n      (fail \"Stream append failed\" {:outcome o, :stream-id stream-id})\n      {:state state,\n       :value {:status :refused, :outcome o, :stream-id stream-id}})))\n\n\n(defn handle-put\n  \"Handle :stream/put. Total over the six append outcomes, once the\n   reference verifies.\n   Returns {:value v :state s} on success, {:park true :stream-id id :state s}\n   on `full`. `closed`, `invalid-value` and `transport-error` are errors\n   that name their outcome, as v1's throw on a closed stream did.\n   `refused`, and any outcome outside this contract version, is not a\n   throw: the effect's value is the shaped refusal\n   {:status :refused, :outcome o, :stream-id id} -- data the program\n   reads, the way `poll-link-response` answers a refused link.\n\n   Under the `:running` gate nothing is observed: the put parks as it\n   would on `full`.\"\n  [state effect]\n  (let [stream-id (check-ref! state :stream/put :stream-ref (:stream effect))\n        val (:val effect)]\n    (if (= :running (gate-refuse! state effect))\n      {:park true, :stream-id stream-id, :state state}\n      (apply-put-outcome state stream-id val","numLines":45,"startLine":490,"totalLines":2789}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0165pMDkrW1gCyHxQ2rR4HFi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
