{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cfz3KFC6XwNjcMufkBriS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The report is written to `collab/1792430000000-architect-any-pc-snapshot.report.md`. No code or docs were edited; the one throwaway JVM probe namespace I used to count the corpus was deleted, and git shows only untracked collab files.\n\n**What I found**\n\n- **The owner's main claim holds.** Every instruction boundary of the semantic-register VM is a canonical state `⟨A, pc, W↾L(pc), E, K⟩`. The kernel already materializes it at fuel exhaustion, and `vm/step` is the one-fuel case. The register pairing is injective over `L(p)` at every pc because linear scan keeps overlapping intervals in distinct slots, and the stack kernel's operand stack at pc `p` is the existing per-pc layout plus the instruction's own operands. Both are checks for the harness, not theorems.\n- **One sentence in the argument is wrong.** \"Performing it is the driver's job\" is true only under the custody gate. The ungated step performs the observe half of a put, next, or FFI call inside the step. The conclusion still stands because a step is atomic, so I restated it that way in the amendment text.\n- **The ready-queue rule is scheduler state.** A woken entry is a performed effect's result that lives in neither a pending nor a window. The engine never leaves one at rest, so I recommend keeping the refusal and crossing it with one step rather than adding a `:ready` row.\n- **Nothing else outside the world appears at a non-parked pc.** Call ids and park ids derive from the carried counter. Op-ids and custody belong to phase 7 and are orthogonal.\n\n**What must change.** One new state kind `:run`, one root kind `:running`, validator rules for a window equal to `L(pc)` with a legal body-start pc, the lift's control branch becoming a kind, and a stepping driver in the harness. Numbering, discharge, and the tail seam are untouched. The real obstructions are per lane. The register kernel refuses a primitive in a live register, which at any pc is every boundary between loading an operator and calling it.\n\n**Cost and order.** The reference-lane half is about 3.5 days including reviews. The cross-engine half is another 4. I recommend slice 6d after phase 7 and before phase 8, with the cross-engine half deferred.\n\n**Verdict: NOT READY** as a slice, pending two owner questions. First, whether the de Bruijn kernels actually die at phase 8. The brief says so, but the frozen design's phase 8 lists the compilers and resolvers for deletion, not the kernels, and that decides whether the cross-engine half is dead work. Second, whether a running root may enter phase 7's custody path. The design amendment itself is READY."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":528,"cache_read_input_tokens":263934,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":528},"output_tokens":686,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7716a8d-bcb9-4b49-9ad0-ed6a5daed388","uuid":"31f01bd8-28e9-49aa-968d-5cadc5f73a4a","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:59:49.971Z","request_id":"req_011Cfz3KEq29w7WHCr5bwoE6"}
